  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "---\ndescription: \"Knowledge-work role skills for DeepSeek Harness: 225 skills across 22 switchable role plugins, ported from anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins.\"\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-knowledge-work",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) plugin that adds\n225 knowledge-work skills across 22 independently switchable role rows — sales,\nsmall business, finance, legal, data, engineering, design, marketing, operations,\nproduct, customer support, HR, bio-research, productivity, PDF reading, enterprise\nsearch, plugin authoring, plus Apollo, brand-voice, Common Room, Slack, and Zoom."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-knowledge-work",
      "text": "The skills come from Anthropic's open-source\n[anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins](https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins)\n(Apache-2.0); see [ATTRIBUTION.md](ATTRIBUTION.md) for what was ported and how."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- DeepSeek Harness `>= 0.2.1-rc.2 < 0.3.0` (declared as `engines.dsh`).\n- A preset that exposes skill discovery and loading (the default presets do)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Plugins page (Desktop / Web)",
      "text": "Open **Plugins**, choose to install a package from GitHub, and enter:\n\n```text\ngithub:AlbertZJ/dsh-knowledge-work\n```\n\nThe bundle is enabled right after installation. Its details page lists the 22 role\nrows, each with its own switch."
    },
    {
      "section": "CLI",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:AlbertZJ/dsh-knowledge-work\ndsh --profile web --dump-config   # the layer appears as \"# == dsh-knowledge-work\"\n```\n\nNo install-time build permission is needed: `lib/` is committed to this repository\nand the package declares no `prepare` script, so pnpm has nothing to allowlist.\n\nPin a commit for reproducible installs:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:AlbertZJ/dsh-knowledge-work#<commit-sha>\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "From npm (after publishing)",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-knowledge-work\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "From a local checkout (development)",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile dev add /absolute/path/to/dsh-knowledge-work\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use the skills",
      "text": "Enable the **Knowledge-work skills** bundle in **Plugins**, then turn roles on or\noff in the bundle's details page. Each role is a separate plugin row: switching\none off unloads its provider and removes its skills from the catalog without\ntouching the other rows. The switches persist in the profile patch layer."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use the skills",
      "text": "A skill whose folder name appears in more than one role gets a `<role>-<skill>`\nprefix so names stay stable when neighbouring rows are switched off — for\nexample `sales-account-research` and `sales-call-prep` (the same skill names also\nexist in Common Room).\n\nSkills are loaded on demand by the model through the skill tool; their bodies are\nnot part of every request until selected."
    },
    {
      "section": "Roles",
      "text": "| Row | Skills | Source |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Bio research | 6 | first-party |\n| Plugin management | 2 | first-party |\n| Customer support | 5 | first-party |\n| Data | 10 | first-party |\n| Design | 7 | first-party |\n| Engineering | 10 | first-party |\n| Enterprise search | 5 | first-party |\n| Finance | 8 | first-party |\n| Human resources | 9 | first-party |\n| Legal | 9 | first-party |\n| Marketing | 8 | first-party |\n| Operations | 9 | first-party |\n| PDF viewer | 1 | first-party |\n| Product management | 8 | first-party |\n| Productivity | 4 | first-party |\n| Sales | 36 | first-party |\n| Small business | 44 | first-party |\n| Apollo | 3 | partner-built |\n| Brand voice | 3 | partner-built |\n| Common Room | 6 | partner-built |\n| Slack | 2 | partner-built |\n| Zoom | 30 | partner-built |\n| **Total** | **225** | 252 `SKILL.md` files incl. nested sub-documents |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Roles",
      "text": "Partner-built rows need their vendor's connector (Apollo, Common Room, Slack,\nZoom). Without it the skill still loads and explains the workflow, but it cannot\nread or write partner data. Brand-voice works from uploaded material."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "```text\ndsh-knowledge-work/\n├── cordis.patch.yml     # bundle layer: one group row + 22 role rows\n├── lib/                 # built entries (index.js + one <role>.js per role)\n├── assets/<role>/<skill>/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "`cordis.patch.yml` inserts each role as its own Loader row named\n`dsh-knowledge-work/<role>`. Each entry registers a skill provider with the\n`skills` service and discovers `<role>/<skill>/SKILL.md` under `assets/` at\nruntime. The package `exports` map serves the role subpaths and their locale\nfiles, which is how the Plugins page reads row titles without running the code."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "Not ported: upstream `.mcp.json` connectors, slash commands, sub-agents, and\nplugin settings. See [ATTRIBUTION.md](ATTRIBUTION.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm run build    # tsc -> lib/types, tsdown -> lib/*.js, then remove lib/types\npnpm run verify   # counts, locale pairing, patch rows, and exports\n```\n\n`lib/` is committed: git installs fetch sources and do not build them, so rebuild\nand commit `lib/` together with any `src/` change."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "Plugin code is MIT ([LICENSE](LICENSE)). The skill assets under `assets/` keep\ntheir upstream licenses: Apache-2.0 for first-party skills\n([kwp-LICENSE.txt](kwp-LICENSE.txt)) and the partner license for partner-built\nskills. See [ATTRIBUTION.md](ATTRIBUTION.md). The package's SPDX license\nexpression is `(MIT AND Apache-2.0)`."
    }
  ],
